      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several issues hurting understandability:\n1. Many unused data provider methods and helpers from other tests clutter the class\n2. Unnecessary imports\n3. The data table has no column labels and is packed on one line\n4. `Long` wrapper types are used with `.longValue()` unnecessarily — can use `long` primitives\n5. The test verifies that `withTaiSeconds` replaces only seconds while preserving nanoseconds, but this intent isn't communicated\n\nLet me write the improved test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused data providers and helper methods, uses primitive `long` parameters instead of boxed `Long`, formats the data table with aligned column labels, and adds clear assertion messages — making the test's intent immediately obvious."
